{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-116412",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The frequency $f$ is inversely proportional to the string length $L,$ so we have\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{k}{L},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that when the string length is $L=0.65\\,\\text{m},$ the frequency of the string is $f=280\\,\\text{hz}.$ We can use this information to solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}280 & =\\frac{k}{0.65} \\\\ 280\\cdot 0.65 & =k \\\\ 182 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now have the equation\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{182}{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can use this equation to find the frequency when the string's length is reduced by $9\\,cm,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{182}{0.65-0.09}=\\frac{182}{0.56}=325\n$$\n\nTherefore, the frequency of the string when $L=0.56\\,cm$ is $f=325\\,hz.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
